WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:08.440
My name's Tetsunosuke Sasaki and I'm tied up like a hog.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.740
Been stuck like this for two weeks straight.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.570
Somebody get me outta here, yo.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.610
Outta here, yo.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:20.410
Collar grabbed, knife in the face, letter torn up, and shunned.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.050
Been abused and tied up like a hog.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.920
Been abused and strung up like a log.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.060
Been stuck like this for two weeks straight.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.140
Somebody get me outta here, yo.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.230
Outta here, yo.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.640
Tied up and almost killed, yo.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.520
But then my ass was saved.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:47.650
My tied-up ass was saved, but then he kicked me off.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.940
Tied up and almost killed, yo.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.340
But then my ass was saved.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.950
My tied-up ass was saved, but then he kicked me off.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.470
My tied-up ass is falling.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:05.070
If I fall, it's over.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.830
Been stuck like this for two weeks straight.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.090
Somebody get me outta here, yo.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.130
Outta here, yo.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.710
Hey, this is supposed to be a serious arc.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.720
Cut this shit out, yo.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.860
Out, yo.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.010
Yeah.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.890
Really. Well, then.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:03.640
Time to do things my way.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.070
Show me what you got, Vice Chief.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:08.790
You're first.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.800
Let's see if you can

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:16.460
take down the Joi patriot known as the White Yaksha.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.300
We brats have to stick together.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.730
But if you still want to kill him, go ahead.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:27.500
Huh?

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.510
You really killed him?!

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:34.700
You told me to kill him!

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.600
Wrong.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.140
I have the hostage!

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.030
Way to hang in there.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:46.100
Go crazy!

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.900
Thornies!

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:53.910
<b>Letter From Thorny</b>

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:55.540
It was a feint!

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.380
Pay them no heed!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.490
Kill them and the terrorists!

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.730
Ch-Chief!

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:13.840
The windshield is cracked!

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.910
And we can't see anything through the smoke!

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:18.470
Cut 'em down!

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.540
Where are they?! Where did they go?!

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:31.750
They're hiding in the smoke!

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.010
I got it!

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:42.700
We can escape while the police are killing each other!

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.790
How?

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.160
We can't see anything in this smoke!

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:46.950
The hole!

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.790
We can escape through the hole that was opened by the explosion!

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.180
And one!

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.530
And two!

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:00.810
And three!

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.600
Wait!

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.600
And four!

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:05.060
It's an SM batting cage down here!

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:03.780
And five!

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.060
Six.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:06.310
Seven.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.960
We got a total sadist batting down here!

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:07.640
Eight.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:08.960
Nine.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.780
I've never heard of an SM batting cage!

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.230
Ten.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:16.380
And we got another one starting a rally!

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.820
Hey, what kind of game is this?!

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.040
Some new SM sport?!

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:24.240
And 19, 20, 21,

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.480
22, 23,

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.270
24.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.400
Th-The stairs!

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.970
The Mimawarigumi isn't watching them right now!

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.630
-Hurry up!

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.630
-And one.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:32.590
And two.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:33.880
And three.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.180
And four.

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:36.550
And five.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:37.990
And six.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:40.420
Wait! It's an anpan factory over here!

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.160
And seven.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:40.750
And eight.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:41.550
Turn back!

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:41.880
And nine.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.810
Head for the pole outside!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.180
And ten.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.440
Huh?

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.310
And one.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:49.950
And two.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.440
And three.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.140
We can't use it!

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:56.230
And four...

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.440
The gorilla keeps sliding up and down!

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.360
He's enjoying the stimulation to his crotch!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:00.910
What the hell do we do?!

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:03.190
There's nowhere to run!

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:04.700
Fire.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.710
But we won't be able to tell friend from foe!

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.310
It doesn't matter.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:11.340
Every moving body is a foe!

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.710
I can see black uniforms!

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:14.390
Fire!

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.180
Wait!

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.470
The Shinsengumi have already been defeated.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.210
Is anyone moving?

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.010
Nobody.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.260
There's one friendly...

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.320
Hijika...

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.760
A grenade!

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.110
Evasive maneuvers! Quick!

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.420
Can't pull up! Mayday! Mayday!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.450
Eject! Hurry!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:27.140
Looks like they're finished over there.

00:07:27.140 --> 00:07:28.880
We should also be...

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:32.620
It's not over.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:38.440
Never sheathe your sword

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.720
before you've dispatched your target.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.640
Isn't that right, killer?

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:50.230
You're better at killing buildings than people.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:56.400
I don't carry a sheath.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:01.170
Maybe you have a good place to stick my sword?

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:09.480
Don't get too worked up.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.820
You aren't my target.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:17.560
Sorry, but I took the last one from you.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:27.230
You and your big sword

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.090
belong in there.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.270
The perfect sheath to rest

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.360
our dull edge.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.470
Ch-Chief!

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:52.500
The building collapsed!

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.250
It's one thing after another!

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:55.500
What's going on?!

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.500
Help...

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.870
Summon reinforcements!

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:04.220
Hurry!

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:14.560
Ch-Chief!

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.310
The terrorists have been tied up!

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.820
<b>We surrender.</b>

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.820
They've given themselves up.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:23.320
H-However, we don't see the Shinsengumi anywhere!

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:25.820
No, they're lying on the roof!

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:28.420
Wait, look!

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:32.330
These are Mimawarigumi officers in Shinsengumi uniforms!

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.380
W-We can't find them!

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:38.030
The Shinsengumi and the hostage have vanished!

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:44.300
I see.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.820
They've likely disguised themselves as Mimawarigumi officers

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:49.670
to fool our advance force

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:53.350
and trick our helicopter into shooting our own men.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:58.100
But since there wasn't much space on the roof,

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.590
we can tell the inspectors

00:10:00.590 --> 00:10:04.610
that the Joi were responsible for everything.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.810
And while the Shinsengumi

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:10.470
were responsible for instigating the fight,

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.560
the Mimawarigumi attacked first.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.620
The responsibility is all yours.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.760
What do you think?

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:21.110
The crisis has been averted,

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:23.380
and there's enough credit to go around.

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:29.390
Why don't you call this a draw and back down?

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:34.380
How about it, Chief?

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.900
Secure the terrorists.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.590
That will do.

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:44.400
You can have the hostage.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.010
This crisis is over.

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:54.210
You have my gratitude, Chief.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:11:01.170
No, we will both be working hard to keep the peace in Edo.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:06.770
Yeah, we'll try not to get in the way of your elite asses.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:08.170
Don't be so humble.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:10.760
You are just as elite.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:18.680
An elite thorn in my side.

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:29.220
Toshi, are you sure about leaving the terrorists with them?

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:30.830
Don't worry.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:35.670
They won't kill people who have surrendered.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.710
I'll put in a word with Matsudaira about their punishment.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.070
But everyone will be talking about the Mimawarigumi now.

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:45.210
They took all the glory.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.200
That's not true.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.060
After all,

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.990
we landed ourselves the jackpot.

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:56.110
Isn't that right, White Yaksha?

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.510
That's former White Yaksha!

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.380
I saved your asses back there,

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:00.720
and now you're turning on me?!

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.950
I knew there was something fishy about you,

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.250
but I never dreamed that you were

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.260
a big-name Joi like Katsura.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:08.860
Former big name!

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:12.490
You know that I'm a model citizen now!

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:15.540
We can charge him with attempted murder.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.490
He kicked Tetsu off the roof.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.080
Okay, fine!

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.130
So I'm a former Joi!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.500
But so is this boy here!

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:25.790
Right, Tetsu-kun?

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:28.380
If you start digging into the past, everyone will look like a criminal!

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:30.510
If you're gonna arrest me, you better arrest him!

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:32.170
He's right!

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:34.120
Allow me to take responsibility!

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.510
I will commit seppuku!

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:37.140
What?!

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:40.040
This crisis was my fault!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.040
No, er, wait!

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:42.640
That wasn't my goal here!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.010
I was afraid to tell everyone,

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:48.590
to tell the vice chief, that I was a former Joi.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:53.150
But my secret led to this mess!

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:55.610
I knew nothing!

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:58.240
I envy you.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:02.520
So please don't run away from your brother!

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:04.590
I thought I could offer you advice,

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:09.170
<b>Tamegoro Hijikata</b>

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:08.430
but I couldn't even deliver your letter!

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:11.510
Not to your brother...

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.470
Not to mine...

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.480
You can always deliver another one.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.670
And this time, you can write it yourself.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:24.000
Didn't you promise that you

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.810
were going to become stronger than me?

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.940
It's your turn now.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:32.690
You might not get the message to your brother.

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:40.000
But your dirty bros here can hear you loud and clear.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:43.750
Yeah, but some of them probably can't read.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:53.010
Tetsu, we'll always be waiting for your letter.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:55.450
Never forget that.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.050
Vice Chief!

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:00.620
Hey, Toshi!

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:03.640
Toshi!

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:20.160
Fishing in a pile of rubble?

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.420
You're pretty whack,

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.440
Mr. Triple Threat.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:30.250
So? Catch anything?

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:31.540
Yes,

00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:34.300
using cheap bait.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:35.920
But I released my catch.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:38.930
Since it would have been a waste to devour it now.

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.010
Are you sure?

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:47.300
Don't you owe it to the Bakufu heads who are backing you?

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:54.290
I have no intention of starting a turf war on broken land.

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:57.950
The Sasaki family is doomed to fall.

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:01.300
In that case, I will continue to use what bait I can.

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:05.450
If he can provide me entertainment, so much the better.

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.710
I now know that there are some dirty fish

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:13.040
waiting out there in this sea of rubble.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.970
So you're saving the best for last?

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.440
I'm sure we'll meet again.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:28.280
Once we clear the rubble from this land,

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:32.940
we get to see how the fish act out of water.

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.500
I can't wait.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.240
Man, why do I have to do this?

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.640
Don't say that!

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:50.540
I'm the one who vouched for your innocence!

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:52.890
I was innocent to begin with!

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:55.050
I saved your asses back there!

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:58.410
Please! You're the only person I can ask!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:00.220
I'll pay you!

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:05.900
I finally finished my letter.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:06.510
Huh?

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.700
This time, I'm going to deliver it!

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.020
Who's the letter for?

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:15.480
The vice chief wrote a letter to my brother for my sake.

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:23.780
<b>Tamegoro Hijikata</b>

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.050
So it's my turn now...

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:19.490
Huh? A letter for a dead person?

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:21.810
The hell is wrong with you?

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:23.780
What's the point?

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:27.700
Please, I want to return the favor.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:31.400
So I must tell his brother that the vice chief is doing well.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.860
You must be joking.

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:35.020
This is so funny it's sad.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:38.550
Uh, I believe the vice chief's brother's grave is over...

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:39.680
Huh?

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:41.720
Somebody's already there.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.450
Oh? This is unusual.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:49.580
Normally, there's only one other person who comes to visit.

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:52.780
Huh? A-Are you his brother's...?

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.570
Oh, I'm, well...

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:58.980
Oh, that letter.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.500
I understand now.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:04.070
You came to deliver his letter.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:08.830
He always leaves his letters here without a word.

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:11.330
Huh? You mean the vice chief?

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:14.000
Yes, once every month.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:17.340
When my husband was still alive, he always looked

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.840
forward to Toshi's letters.

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:23.110
Th-Then the vice chief and his brother were talking to one another?

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:24.750
Only through their letters.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:27.850
The last time they met was many years ago.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:30.850
Yes, I believe it was the day before he left

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:32.350
for Edo with Kondo-san and his friends.

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:34.850
We hadn't heard from him in years,

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.510
but then he suddenly showed up.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.360
But he refused to talk to his brother.

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:44.360
They ate dinner in silence and drank in silence.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:48.300
Toshi, send letters.

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:51.950
And then he left in silence.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:57.340
After that, he would send a letter every month.

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.920
His brother was so thrilled.

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:04.270
He couldn't see, yet he was always so eager.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:08.250
Has Toshi's letter come yet? Has Toshi's letter come yet?

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:15.790
That's why I continue to read these letters for him.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:25.810
Though he's still a stubborn and tight-lipped boy in his letters.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:29.460
I suppose his brother, blind as he was, could see something in him.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.490
Their bond needed no words.

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:38.000
No, I'm sure that brothers, family,

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:44.690
just want to hear that you're still alive.

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:53.070
Dear, you have another letter from Toshi.

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:55.240
Here it is.

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:57.100
Oh?

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:02.270
You failed to deliver your letter again.

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:03.660
Are you okay with that?

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:05.290
It's okay.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.920
Now that I've seen his letters, I would be

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:08.440
too embarrassed to show his brother my letter.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:14.790
The vice chief and his brother were always linked.

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:19.130
After hearing that, I'm content.

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:39.270
<b>Greater Edo Hospital</b>

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:50.280
<b>From Thorny</b>

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.370
Damn.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:22:00.950
<b>To Thorny</b>

00:19:58.200 --> 00:20:00.490
Can't think of anything to write.

00:22:31.890 --> 00:22:35.230
Ask Mr. Ginpachi!

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:39.070
Okay. I'll read the next postcard.

00:22:39.070 --> 00:22:41.910
This is from someone with the pen name Akari-san.

00:22:41.910 --> 00:22:43.270
Hello, Mr. Ginpachi.

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:45.260
There's a question that's been bugging me.

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:47.670
Hijikata-san said that he would quit

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:51.810
smoking in the Ooey-gooey Balls episode, right?

00:22:52.130 --> 00:22:56.970
But I keep seeing him with white sticks in his mouth.

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:59.140
Why is that?

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:01.530
Is he trying to maintain his image?

00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:03.980
Are you the same, Mr. Ginpachi?

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:06.930
I don't have a problem with smoking,

00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:09.560
but please let me know if there is a reason.

00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:12.390
Okay, here's your answer.

00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:16.240
People who try to quit smoking always fail.

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:19.860
I'm sure that Hiroshi Tachi will prove that soon,

00:23:19.860 --> 00:23:22.240
so keep an eye out.

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:26.100
By the way, this is a lollipop in my mouth.

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:28.390
Did anyone forget?

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:32.990
Welcome to Who Wants to Be a Madaonaire.

00:23:32.990 --> 00:23:35.880
The unemployed and middle-aged Taizo Hasegawa

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:39.380
will be attempting to win an unheard of amount of money!

00:23:40.110 --> 00:23:40.850
Next time:

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:42.550
Madaodog Madaonaire.

00:23:41.590 --> 00:23:44.930
<b>Madaodog Madaonaire</b>

00:23:42.880 --> 00:23:44.340
Is that your final answer?

00:23:44.930 --> 00:23:48.930
<b>Trace back through your hazy memories for a chance to turn your life around!!</b>

00:23:48.930 --> 00:23:54.940
<b>What will the Madao inside Madao declare to be his final answer?!</b>
